    "body": "## Summary\n\nFinal commit of ADR-043. Marks the ADR as Implemented with the PNG-verified visible delta.\n\n**Confirmed**: 1px gray line under `.vector-page-toolbar-container` appears in AFTER screenshot, absent in BEFORE.\n\n## The ADR-039 lesson working\n\nDuring Commit 2's PNG verification, the initial paint drew the FULL shadow rectangle. Because the toolbar has a transparent background, the inner shadow region showed through as a **20px gray band behind the tab labels** — not the predicted 1px line.\n\n**Root cause**: my paint code didn't clip the shadow. CSS Backgrounds 3 §7.1: *\"An outer box-shadow casts a shadow as if the border-box were opaque. The shadow is drawn outside the border edge only: it is clipped inside the border-box.\"*\n\n**Fix**: even-odd fill rule clip of (shadow_rect, box_rect) — leaves only the L-shaped exterior region visible (~6 lines). Re-verification passed.\n\n**This is exactly why ADR-039 was reverted in the pre-chat session**, and why ADR-040/041/042/043 all gate merge on PNG verification. A bug that unit tests can't catch was caught by the visual gate.\n\n## Docs updated\n\n- ADR-043 → Implemented with full Implementation section (including the bug-and-fix note)\n- ADR-034: Post-ADR-043 note (shadow draw order relative to background-image)\n- README row 043\n- CHANGELOG entry\n\n## Test count\n\n- 551 cases / 2125 assertions all pass\n- Documentation only; no code changes\n\nRefs #212",
